AND THE SCHEMA CANNOT TELL YOU WHICH FORM YOU ARE FILING. dph2018.xsd and
dph2020.xsd are BYTE-IDENTICAL apart from their own documentation string
("DPH2018" vs "DPH2020"). The tlačivá are not: r18 is the § 81 deregistration
liability in the 2018 vzor, and the § 48ca ods. 2 / § 48d ods. 15 / § 48e
ods. 3 a 8 daň in the 2020 one, which folded § 81 into r01-r04. A 2018-vintage
return therefore validates PERFECTLY against the 2020 schema while carrying a
number on a row that means something else. Only the tlačivo separates them,
which is why the validity windows above are recorded here and enforced in the
version records rather than inferred from a file.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Not for the reason it used to give. This file previously
claimed these schemas "carry NO version attribute and NO Ucinnost line" and
that "the filename is ours rather than the ministry's". Both are false, found
on 2026-09-08 while fetching the older vintages:

  * each file stamps itself in an xsd:documentation annotation — dph2021.xsd
    says "DPHv21 v1.2" and dph2025.xsd says "DPHv25". The 2021 one carries a
    REVISION as well as a vintage, which is more than the KV schemas manage;
  * the filenames are Finančná správa's own. dph2012.xsd, dph2018.xsd and
    dph2020.xsd were fetched from
    https://ekr.financnasprava.sk/Formulare/XSD/ at exactly those names, and
    the refresh procedure below has always fetched by filename.

The pinning is still right, for a narrower reason: a stamp is not a guarantee.
"DPHv21 v1.2" would not necessarily become v1.3 if the file were revised in
place, and nothing validates the annotation — it is a comment. So the digest
remains the only thing that detects a silent revision. What changed is that it
is no longer the only thing that identifies the vzor.

⚠️ AND A STAMP DOES NOT ALWAYS SEPARATE TWO VINTAGES. dph2018.xsd and
dph2020.xsd are STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL — same elements, same types; the entire
difference is the DPH2018 / DPH2020 string. Yet the forms differ: row 18 is the
§ 81 deregistration liability in the 2018 vzor and the § 48ca/§ 48d/§ 48e daň
in the 2020 one, and § 81 moves up into rows 01/03. So a 2018-shaped return
validates perfectly against the 2020 schema while several rows mean something
else. Schema validation cannot catch a wrong-vintage SK VAT return; only the
tlačivo distinguishes them. Anyone adding the pre-2021 vintages needs to know
that before trusting a green validation.

